# Trivy vulnerability waivers (triaged 2026-09-10)
#
# Both findings below are reported against packages that exist ONLY as
# build-provenance metadata inside wheel-embedded SBOM files
# (*.dist-info/sboms), never as installed runtime packages.
#
# Evidence verified at triage time:
# - `uv.lock` contains neither msgpack nor setuptools (grep count = 0)
# - inside the built image: `python -c "import msgpack/setuptools"` fails with
#   ModuleNotFoundError, and `find / -name "*msgpack*" -o -name "*setuptools*"`
#   returns no dist-info directories (only pip's vendored copy at
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/msgpack, which is part
#   of pip itself, not an installed msgpack distribution)
# - Trivy JSON reports both findings with "AnalyzedBy": "sbom" and no FilePath,
#   attributed to a base-image layer
#
# Re-evaluate these waivers when the base image or the producing wheels are
# updated (pip vendors msgpack; upstream wheels embed their build SBOMs).

# msgpack 1.1.2 (build-time dep recorded in wheel-embedded SBOM; fixed in 1.2.1)
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools 70.3.0 (build-time dep recorded in wheel-embedded SBOM; fixed 78.1.1)
CVE-2025-47273